WEBVTT

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:10.410
Um,

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.830
good morning. This is Futaba.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:17.770
Today... Today, your two cheery co-hosts
will cheerfully bring you today's program!

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:21.610
N-Now, we'll start with some free talk...

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.940
Um...

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.920
So, I woke up early this morning!

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.360
And then, when I started making
a sunny-side up egg for breakfast,

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.930
something surprising happened!

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.540
G-Guess what!

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.170
There were two egg yolks!

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:40.530
Um... It tasted...

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.380
normal, I guess.

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:47.550
I had some bread, too.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:54.300
Well, this is pretty much
how a radio show works, right?

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.020
Right, Korori-chan?

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:03.840
I was surprised when the producer suddenly
asked us to be on a web radio show, though.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:10.160
<i>I need a fresh, new program to publicize</i> Bodhisattvon<i>!</i>

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:11.860
<i>Right...</i>

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:17.140
<i>So I want your three fresh faces to be in it!</i>

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.240
<i>You want the three of us...</i>

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.920
<i>...to be radio personalities?</i>

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:24.020
Even though Pipo exploded,

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:28.680
it sounded like I would still be
a regular part of the recording sessions.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:34.020
I'm sure you'll surprise the world
with your conversational mastery-koro!

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.920
It'll be fine, won't it?

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:43.150
Nothing to worry about, right, Korori-chan?

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:16.950
My first radio show!

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.970
This is the perfect chance to show
the whole world my strawberry persona!

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:24.930
Hi! I'm Moesaki Ichigo!

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:27.210
Coming to you again from Planet Strawberry—

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:31.800
Jeez, I was just about to get into it.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.180
Dad!

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.190
"I started following your tweets."

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:43.310
What?!

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:46.320
Th-This Kagawa Gengoro guy...

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.300
Don't tell me that's Dad!

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:50.820
Wait, are all of these...

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.330
my relatives?!

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:02.960
A-All my relatives are reading about my daily life...?

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:05.780
Well, I've got nothing
to be embarrassed about!

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:08.080
I was prepared for this much at least—

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:13.310
"Dear Ichigoron-san, thank you for your loyal support of my daughter.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:17.560
Please let me know
if you're ever in Kagawa."

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:19.680
He's replying to my fans!

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:23.640
Jeez, he's telling them every little detail!

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:27.270
Hang on, he uploaded pictures of me from kindergarten?!

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:30.220
And this is definitely the
neighborhood pachinko parlor!

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:34.160
My persona...

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:35.150
<b>Little Witches Honyanya</b>

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:38.210
Y-Yes, I'd like to take on new challenges!
<b>Little Witches Honyanya</b>

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:38.700
Rin-chan, you started out
as a child actor, right?
<b>Little Witches Honyanya</b>

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.860
Rin-chan, you started out
as a child actor, right?

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:45.890
Yes, my parents were concerned that I was too introverted

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:49.550
and thought it might help
if I joined a theater troupe.

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:53.620
But now you're a popular seiyuu,

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:56.760
so I'd say you're living up to your parents' expectations.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:59.470
Oh no, I'm still not that good!

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:04.930
Um, okay then, Rin-chan, how about a message on everyone's behalf?

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:05.980
Oh, okay!

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:07.970
Um...

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:13.720
We'll keep doing our best,
so please give us your support!

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:19.010
Okay, thank you!

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:22.540
Your comments are always
so nice and natural, Rin-chan.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:28.160
Even though you've been in the business for so long,
it's as if you're just a normal girl.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:29.670
Normal...?

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:33.130
Well then, everyone, thank you for today!

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:35.350
Thank you!

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:37.020
Rin-chan!

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:41.060
By the way, you're going to be on a new radio show, aren't you?

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:42.560
Y-Yes!

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:44.260
I'm looking forward to it!

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:49.170
I don't really have anything interesting to say, though...

00:05:49.170 --> 00:05:53.000
On the radio, you just need someone
who can keep normal conversation going.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.320
You'll be fine!

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.670
Normal, huh?

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:06.330
At the diner the other day,
I ordered a salmon roe rice bowl—

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:08.230
Oops...

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:12.420
Shiodome-san! I'm sorry! Good morning!

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:16.260
Morning. Flustered as usual, I see?

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:22.600
Oh, Ichinose-san, you'll be on Shiodome-san's radio show next week.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:23.800
Huh?!

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.720
Your new show is starting soon, right?

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:28.730
So you can come on mine and promote it.

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:32.210
Thank you very much!

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:36.570
Wait, your radio show is live, isn't it?

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:38.110
That's right.

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:40.450
So you can't make any mistakes!

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:44.080
B-But this'll be my first time
doing anything live!

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:46.610
Don't worry.

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:48.710
I'll make sure to back you up.

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:50.650
O... kay...

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:55.240
I have another recording session
I must attend, so I can't go with you.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:07:00.720
But Moesaki-san and Kohana-san
will be there with you, so you'll be fine.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.260
What? Ichigo and Rin-chan will be there?

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:03.970
Yes.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:07.990
Ichinose-san.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:10.770
Let me tell you a proverb
about doing radio work.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.400
Please do!

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:17.900
You can't erase a careless remark once it hits the airwaves, but...

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:19.650
Uh-huh.

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:22.910
...you can erase the person who said it.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.750
That wasn't very nice.

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:36.800
...which means, we're going
to be on the radio! As guests!

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:39.970
So that's why you wanted to go out all of a sudden...

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:43.930
But you can't make mistakes
on a live broadcast!

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.900
We're just promoting our show, right?

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:50.770
But we won't get the script
for it until the day of.

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:54.400
I guess it's not like a recording session.

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:57.090
Are you ready to order?

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:59.350
Um, I'll have the broiled miso lunch plate.

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:00.720
All right.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:02.410
No, no, no!

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:04.380
That's not what I meant.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:08.410
I'd like a strawberry bagel combo, please!

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.040
O-Okay...

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:11.770
Ichigo-san, you're amazing!

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:15.590
I see! You're going to use your persona to get through the live broadcast!

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:19.010
N-Not really...

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:22.260
This isn't just a personality
I made up for the radio.

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:26.180
I wonder if I'll know how to talk
with your persona, Ichigo-san.

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:28.100
Do you want to brainstorm
some jokes first?

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:31.120
Quit acting like we're comedians!

00:08:35.020 --> 00:08:36.860
Good morning!

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:39.310
There you are.

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:46.170
The staff of a radio show is usually
unexpectedly small, compared to TV shows-koro.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:47.670
First is the director.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:50.910
He gives instructions
and supervises the operation-koro.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.360
Next is the mixer.

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:56.420
He switches between the talk
and music portions of the program

00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:58.210
and adjusts the voice levels.

00:08:58.210 --> 00:08:58.230
Definitely an essential role-koro.
and adjusts the voice levels.

00:08:58.230 --> 00:09:00.670
Definitely an essential role-koro.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.720
The broadcast writer doesn't
just write the script for the show,

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:10.350
he also occasionally goes into the studio with the personalities to give them topics to talk about-koro.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:13.160
Looking forward to working with you!

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.070
Oh, good morning!

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:26.860
It's our guest, Tamura Yukari-san!

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:28.370
Hello.

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:28.390
Looking forward to working with you!
Hello.

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:30.080
Looking forward to working with you!

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.080
<i>T-Tamura Yukari-san?!</i>

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:34.940
Welcome. Right this way.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:36.580
Good morning.

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:38.630
Good morning!

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:40.610
We'll be part of today's Publicity Corner.

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:42.450
I'm Moesaki Ichigo!

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:44.050
I'm Ichinose Futaba.

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:45.600
I'm Kohana Rin.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.570
Nice to meet you!

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:48.780
You too!

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:56.240
Radio Gonzo, 7 p.m.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:01.580
It's Shiodome Hikari's
Hikari Radio Wave Station!

00:10:07.780 --> 00:10:08.780
That's true.

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:10.070
Yeah, yeah!

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:12.310
Then let's move on to the next message.

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:13.450
What, already?

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:14.130
Yeah.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:14.930
Fine, I guess.

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:16.080
What's with that attitude?

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:18.640
Hurry, hurry! Read it, read it!

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:22.830
<i>Wow, Tamura Yukari's
got them totally charmed!</i>

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:26.310
<i>Even though they're not following a script,</i>

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:30.850
<i>their conversation keeps flowing, and it's really pulling me in!</i>

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:37.350
<i>Hey, hey, Yukarin,</i>

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:41.900
<i>this is kind of sudden, but would it be okay if
I asked some of my kouhai to come into the studio?</i>

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:44.690
Wow, welcome.

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:50.610
Okay then, let's have Futa-Futa introduce herself first!

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:52.280
F-Futa-Futa?

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:55.250
atafuta
You're always flustered,
so I'm calling you Futa-Futa!

00:10:55.250 --> 00:11:00.980
A VA's first nickname usually sticks with her, doesn't it?

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:01.460
What?

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:03.290
Good luck, Futa-Futa!

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:04.960
Go for it, Futa-Futa!

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:08.090
W-Why are you trying to make it stick?

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:09.760
Come on, come on.

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:12.500
Aren't you here to promote your new radio show?

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:22.230
Uh, um... I-I-I'm the newly-christened F-Futa-Futa, Ichinose Futaba.

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:25.460
O-Our radio show is about to begin...

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:29.680
Um, um, R-Radio Bodhisattvon!

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:32.720
Trying the Patience of Bodhisattvon!

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:36.620
Okay, good work.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:40.550
Was that really good enough
to promote the show?

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:43.630
I have no idea what people
are gonna think about that.

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:48.300
I don't even remember what I said.

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:52.290
Good work today!

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:55.990
Good work today!

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:56.970
Good work.

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:59.930
You girls were really funny.

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:02.940
You think so?

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:05.510
I hope your web radio show goes well.

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:07.440
Yes, we'll give it our best!

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:08.800
We'll work hard!

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:10.860
Have me on your show sometime!

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:11.880
Later.

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:15.240
Thanks for your hard work today!

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:20.290
It would be nice if Tamura-san
came on our radio show, wouldn't it?

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:24.880
Yeah, but then we'd end up being the extras.

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:26.400
That's true.

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:28.590
We shouldn't depend on others at first.

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:31.970
Radio Bodhisattvon is our show!

00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:33.030
Yes!

00:12:33.030 --> 00:12:34.280
You're right.

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:38.020
Let's make our radio show great!

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.240
Good morning...

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:46.060
You're late!

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:50.410
The first floor was a regular storefront, so I didn't notice there was a studio...

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:52.140
Well, there is!

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:54.510
Though it's a pretty small one...

00:12:54.510 --> 00:12:57.810
It's a little different from Shiodome-san's radio show, isn't it?

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:02.160
There are a lot of different types of radio studios, too-koro.

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:06.760
But no matter how small they are, they're all pro studios with professional equipment-koro.

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:08.680
Is that the director?

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:10.790
Where are the writer and mixer?

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:14.640
For this show, the director's going to handle everything.

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:16.120
Wow!

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:18.980
I've heard that this is common
for web radio shows.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:20.190
Wow...

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:22.190
Hmm...

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:24.130
Glad to be working with you today.

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:26.320
Looking forward to working with you!

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:28.460
Here's the script for today.

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:30.920
Wow, it's only a few pages.

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:36.470
It says ten minutes of free talk here, but there's nothing written down...

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:38.830
That's because it's free.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:44.600
<i>You mean you want us to talk like Shiodome-san and Tamura-san did?!</i>

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:46.920
<i>Radio is scary!</i>

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:51.750
How about we start
recording the real thing now?

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:53.190
O-Okay!

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:00.600
All right, we're rolling.

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:04.860
Radio Bodhisattvon:

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:07.930
Trying the Patience of Bodhisattvon!

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:13.500
H-Hello, I'm Ichinose Futaba.

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:17.220
H-Hello, I'm Moesaki Ichigo.

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:19.620
Hello, I'm Kohana Rin.

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:24.500
<i>How exactly am I
supposed to introduce myself?</i>

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:27.270
<i>Huh? Wait, who's going first?</i>

00:14:27.270 --> 00:14:30.250
<i>Going right into introductions
is weird, isn't it?</i>

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:32.760
<i>Don't we need a reason
to start talking about that?</i>

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:34.240
Hm?

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:36.580
What's wrong?

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:38.880
If you don't say something,
we've just got dead air.

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:40.440
<i>S-Sorry!</i>

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:43.900
Um...
Well then!

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:54.270
I-I, Moesaki Ichigo, am here again from
Planet Strawberry in the Strawberry Nebula!

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:56.990
Everyone, let's go!

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:59.010
Um, uh...

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:05.380
M-Moving on, I'm Ichinose Futaba.

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:08.500
I took the train here with my manager today.

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:12.190
After walking for a while from the station, we stopped by a convenience store,
<i>Futaba-san, you can't
let your tone drop like that!</i>

00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:13.940
<i>where I bought a rice ball...</i>

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:15.610
<i>Now, let's read some letters
from you, the listeners.</i>

00:15:15.610 --> 00:15:20.290
Now, let's read some letters
from you, the listeners.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:23.850
Hm? We already have mail even though we're recording the first episode now?

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:28.180
Before a radio show starts, they advertise beforehand

00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:33.000
so that they already have emails and postcards from the listeners for the first episode-koro.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.280
For the first message...

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:36.920
Futaba-san, do the honors.

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:38.280
R-Right!

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:41.450
Um... from Maeda Kosaku-san...

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:44.360
Oh, shoot! That's his real name!

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.890
Um... Radio name, Marine-san from Nerima.

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:48.180
<i>Um... Radio name, Marine-san from Nerima.</i>

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:49.140
<i>Hey...</i>

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:54.210
We've got a question:
"What sports do you like?"

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:56.150
Well, Ichigo-san?

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:58.950
Me? Sumo and stuff?

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:01.120
I mean, um...

00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:04.140
We even get broadcasts of
soccer games on Planet Strawberry!

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:07.310
Oh, you like soccer, Ichigo-san?

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:10.230
On Planet Strawberry, we've got the Kamatamare Strawberries...

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:15.290
<i>The actual taboo words for radio aren't dirty or obscene words that can't be aired.</i>

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:18.210
<i>They're "Nothing in particular"
and "I don't know."</i>

00:16:18.530 --> 00:16:22.740
<i>These are two mediocre remarks that
don't take the conversation anywhere.</i>

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:24.490
<i>They're crappy comments!</i>

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:26.410
What about you, Futaba-san?

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:28.270
Futaba-san?

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:30.710
Huh?! Oh, wh-what was that?

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:33.740
What soccer team do you like?

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:34.230
Huh?

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:36.840
Oh, none in particular...

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:38.040
Huh?! Ah!

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:41.170
F-Futaba...?

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:44.510
Now, on to the next question.

00:16:44.510 --> 00:16:47.240
What kinds of food do you like?

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:48.730
Here it is!

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:51.300
<i>This is where I answer,
"Strawberry sandwiches!"</i>

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:54.480
<i>But then I act all cute and say,</i>

00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:57.170
<i>"Oh, but that would be cannibalism!"</i>

00:16:57.470 --> 00:17:00.620
Personally, I like strawberry daifuku.

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:02.550
I'm good at making them, too.

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:03.940
<i>What?!</i>

00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:06.410
<i>You should've left the
strawberry-related foods for me!</i>

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:08.300
Hm?

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:09.680
You know what...?

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:13.490
<i>Expand?</i>

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:18.170
Rin-chan, do daifuku expand
when you bake them, like mochi?

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:21.230
I don't think so.

00:17:21.230 --> 00:17:23.460
<i>That's not what I meant...</i>

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:26.780
What foods do you like that expand?

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:28.060
<i>What the heck, Futaba?</i>

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:30.410
<i>Who'd wanna know about
the expanding foods we like?</i>

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:33.580
<i>Huh? I just said whatever came to mind to keep the conversation moving...</i>

00:17:33.580 --> 00:17:36.870
<i>Anyway, what expanding foods are there besides bubble gum...?</i>

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:40.780
My favorite expanding food is bubble gum!

00:17:42.730 --> 00:17:46.430
What expanding foods do you like, Ichigo-san?

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:48.570
U-Um... Uh...

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.600
Speaking of expanding...

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:56.920
When you go to check out
the top rugby teams...

00:17:56.920 --> 00:17:58.880
Oh wait, those are the standings!

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:13.120
This is great!

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:25.960
All right, make sure
you tune in next time, too!

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:27.810
See you later!

00:18:28.480 --> 00:18:31.460
<i>Okay, good work.</i>

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:33.290
Thanks for your hard work!

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:36.230
Good job, good job!

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:37.770
Man, that was great!

00:18:38.710 --> 00:18:40.450
Thank you very much!

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:41.520
It was great?

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:42.480
That was?

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:43.910
How should I put it?

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:48.170
Of all the chaotic shows I've ever seen,
this was the best one.

00:18:48.170 --> 00:18:50.350
You girls have real potential!

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:52.350
Potential?

00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:57.150
It <i>was</i> all over the place, though.

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:57.870
All over the place.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:12.010
I feel like it was over before
I even knew what was going on.

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:16.170
But didn't Kaibara-san say it was great?

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:18.460
Can we really believe him?

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:20.770
He's a hard man to understand, huh?

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:22.570
Like the ghost of an alien!

00:19:22.570 --> 00:19:23.180
Huh?

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:25.220
Huh? What's that?

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:27.370
I'm saying he's downright mysterious!

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:29.680
That's not funny.

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:36.310
I think Kaibara-san would be better off
doing one of those surreal comedy sketches.

00:19:36.310 --> 00:19:37.770
Oh? Why do you say that?

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:40.480
In addition to being mysterious, he's hard to understand!

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:41.720
I see!

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:44.290
Huh?

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:48.460
Jeez, is it really that funny?

00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:49.250
Huh?
But what do you like about aliens?

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:49.930
But what do you like about aliens?

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:51.280
<i>That conversation seemed
pretty lively just there.</i>

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:54.820
Their mysterious side, I guess?

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:55.460
Yeah, me too!

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:56.670
They have a strange charm, don't they?

00:19:56.670 --> 00:20:00.210
<i>I hope we can talk
like this on the radio, too.</i>

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:04.860
Isn't it about time?

00:20:04.860 --> 00:20:05.770
Huh?

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:07.010
Oh, right.

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:10.010
<i>If you're looking to sell your car, come to Used Car Center Zongo!</i>

00:20:24.710 --> 00:20:27.500
So that's what kind of scene this was, huh?

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:29.460
I can finally tell now that it's in color.

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:32.450
<i>Napolitan pasta sounds yummy right now.</i>

00:20:32.450 --> 00:20:35.830
Was that all right for the voice of someone with big boobs?

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:37.660
<i>Wait a minute!</i>

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:41.210
<i>Jeez, Reiji, were you even listening?</i>

00:20:41.790 --> 00:20:42.790
<i>I think it was this way...</i>

00:20:43.070 --> 00:20:46.730
Isn't it almost time for Pipo, Futaba-san?

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:49.480
<i>Pipo...</i>

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:56.240
Is that how my voice sounds?

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:59.530
The emotional nuance I was so worried about...

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:02.980
Does it come across here?

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:04.330
<i>Pipooooo!</i>

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:08.750
Hey! I can't see!

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:11.590
The only thing that comes across is that I suck!

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:14.590
It's obvious!

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:18.240
Oh, if that's what you call love,

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:19.580
<i>That light reaches into the universe!</i>

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:26.170
then do it one more time!

00:21:27.960 --> 00:21:29.860
Well, that was lame.

00:21:29.860 --> 00:21:33.090
I thought I was gonna
sound better than that.

00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:33.480
What would we do

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:36.010
Me too...

00:21:36.010 --> 00:21:36.090
Huh?!
What would we do

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:36.910
if there were no tomorrow?

00:21:36.910 --> 00:21:37.850
You too, Rin-chan?

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:38.270
if there were no tomorrow?

00:21:38.270 --> 00:21:40.570
I always feel that way.

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:41.180
Like, there's always some way I could've improved my performance.

00:21:41.180 --> 00:21:44.130
Would we still dare to dream?

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:46.150
Even Rin-chan can relate?

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:46.480
But you know, even if we're not great at acting or being on the radio,

00:21:46.480 --> 00:21:50.310
Save them, shaking at the edge of the colorless sky

00:21:50.310 --> 00:21:51.710
all we can do is work harder!

00:21:51.710 --> 00:21:52.010
Save them, shaking at the edge of the colorless sky

00:21:52.010 --> 00:21:54.280
You're right. We've got the chance to give this our best shot.

00:21:54.280 --> 00:21:54.300
Young unfledged ones, become light!

00:21:54.300 --> 00:21:55.730
You're right. We've got the chance to give this our best shot.

00:21:55.730 --> 00:21:59.350
Kaibara-san said we had potential, too!
Young unfledged ones, become light!

00:21:59.350 --> 00:22:00.980
Didn't you just call him an alien?
Young unfledged ones, become light!

00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:01.820
Didn't you just call him an alien?

00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:05.210
Pipo: Ichinose Futaba
